WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.010 --> 00:00:17.996
The person in the water turned out to be a boy.

2
00:00:19.257 --> 00:00:21.778
He was holding a large basket of mud.

3
00:00:22.499 --> 00:00:26.161
Coughing, Vinnie climbed back onto the tiny island.

4
00:00:26.181 --> 00:00:28.762
“Who are you?”

5
00:00:29.302 --> 00:00:30.143
the boy asked.

6
00:00:30.163 --> 00:00:32.004
“I’m Vinnie.

7
00:00:32.364 --> 00:00:38.246
This is my sister, Mandy,” Vinnie replied, shaking his wet hair.

8
00:00:38.266 --> 00:00:41.748
“Where is your family garden?”

9
00:00:42.248 --> 00:00:43.108
the boy asked.

10
00:00:43.128 --> 00:00:47.690
“We don’t have one,” admitted Vinnie.

11
00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:49.771
“We’re just visiting.

12
00:00:50.231 --> 00:00:51.192
Do you need help?”

13
00:00:52.973 --> 00:00:54.393
The boy thought a moment.

14
00:00:55.454 --> 00:00:56.954
“Yes,” he said.

15
00:00:56.974 --> 00:00:59.095
“Collect mud from the lake.

16
00:00:59.855 --> 00:01:01.096
Then pile it on here.”

17
00:01:02.176 --> 00:01:03.657
He pointed to the island.

18
00:01:05.718 --> 00:01:08.620
He had dark skin and was dressed like Vinnie.

19
00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:11.201
“Why do you need mud?”

20
00:01:11.982 --> 00:01:12.702
Vinnie asked.

21
00:01:13.703 --> 00:01:16.004
The boy looked at them, surprised.

22
00:01:16.024 --> 00:01:20.147
“It helps the crops grow strong,” he said.

23
00:01:20.167 --> 00:01:22.988
“Corn and beans grow best on this soil.

24
00:01:23.929 --> 00:01:26.090
Our corn was very good last year.

25
00:01:27.091 --> 00:01:29.152
So we are making more floating gardens.”

26
00:01:31.252 --> 00:01:32.973
“What a great name!”

27
00:01:33.674 --> 00:01:35.115
Mandy clapped her hands.

28
00:01:36.015 --> 00:01:39.198
The tiny islands did look like floating gardens.

29
00:01:40.058 --> 00:01:41.880
Each one had a different crop.

30
00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:46.483
For the next hour, Vinnie and Mandy helped the boy.

31
00:01:49.325 --> 00:01:51.226
They piled mud on the island.

32
00:01:52.027 --> 00:01:54.188
Mandy smoothed the mud with a stick.

33
00:01:55.069 --> 00:01:56.209
A canoe went by.

34
00:01:56.229 --> 00:01:58.411
“Look, Vinnie!”

35
00:01:59.011 --> 00:01:59.592
she called.

36
00:02:00.512 --> 00:02:04.394
“People use canoes to move from one island to the next.”

37
00:02:04.414 --> 00:02:07.595
“Who are you, little girl?”

38
00:02:08.155 --> 00:02:09.636
someone behind her asked.

39
00:02:10.696 --> 00:02:11.977
Mandy turned around.

40
00:02:13.137 --> 00:02:16.639
A man was sitting in a canoe with a big pile of corn.

41
00:02:17.539 --> 00:02:18.780
He had kind eyes.

42
00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:22.321
“We’re friends of Mandy paused.

43
00:02:23.441 --> 00:02:25.082
She didn’t know the boy’s name.

44
00:02:26.043 --> 00:02:28.123
“Of Mazatl?

45
00:02:28.724 --> 00:02:29.144
I see.

46
00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:31.201
Where is my son now?”

47
00:02:31.761 --> 00:02:32.282
he asked.

48
00:02:32.302 --> 00:02:37.065
“He’s getting mud from the water, sir,” she replied.

49
00:02:38.086 --> 00:02:41.548
Mandy thought Mazatl looked very much like his father.

50
00:02:41.568 --> 00:02:45.150
“Good,” Mazatl’s father nodded.

51
00:02:45.170 --> 00:02:48.052
“Tell Mazatl I will be at the market.

52
00:02:48.913 --> 00:02:51.134
I want to go early to get a good spot.”

53
00:02:52.015 --> 00:02:53.116
He paddled away.

54
00:02:54.777 --> 00:02:58.960
As Mandy watched him leave, she wondered, “Where are we?”

55
00:03:00.692 --> 00:03:04.773
When the boys returned, Mandy told Mazatl what his father said.

56
00:03:04.793 --> 00:03:10.535
“I must hurry and join Papa at the weekly market,” said Mazatl.

57
00:03:10.555 --> 00:03:12.635
“May we come with you?”

58
00:03:13.376 --> 00:03:14.076
asked Vinnie.

59
00:03:14.096 --> 00:03:18.297
“Yes, but come to my house first,” said Mazatl.

60
00:03:18.317 --> 00:03:21.078
“We can take a bath and change our clothes.”

61
00:03:21.098 --> 00:03:26.239
“Thanks, Mazatl,” Mandy said.

62
00:03:26.259 --> 00:03:29.340
“What a great place this is.”

63
00:03:30.312 --> 00:03:31.273
Mazatl nodded.

64
00:03:32.133 --> 00:03:34.655
She really wished she knew where she was.

65
00:03:34.675 --> 00:03:39.958
“Our gods are good to us if we are good to them,” Mazatl said.

66
00:03:39.978 --> 00:03:42.900
“How are you good to the gods?”

67
00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:44.501
Mandy asked.

68
00:03:45.621 --> 00:03:47.582
“We make sacrifices regularly.”

69
00:03:47.602 --> 00:03:50.624
“What kind of sacrifices?”

70
00:03:51.525 --> 00:03:52.205
asked Vinnie.

71
00:03:54.467 --> 00:03:56.628
Mazatl stared at them suspiciously.

72
00:03:57.524 --> 00:04:02.469
“Our Aztec gods are offered only the best sacrifices— humans!”

73
00:04:03.470 --> 00:04:04.592
he said proudly.

74
00:04:04.612 --> 00:04:10.057
“Aztec? We’re in ancient Mexico?”

75
00:04:10.838 --> 00:04:11.859
gasped Mandy.

76
00:04:11.879 --> 00:04:14.522
“Human sacrifices?”

77
00:04:15.183 --> 00:04:15.944
cried Vinnie.
